      "score": 38,
      "reasoning": "This is an objective criterion. The cumulative loss and 2023 maximum are close to the published values, but the reconstruction substantially underestimates the acceleration (19% versus 36%) and gives materially different subperiod rates; it also fails to quantify the required comparison showing glacier loss exceeds Greenland by 18% and Antarctica by more than twofold."
     },
     {
      "index": 1,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.1,
      "score": 34,
      "reasoning": "Mode A. The agent quantitatively identifies the major absolute contributors and closely reproduces Alaska (~22.6%), combined Canadian Arctic (~18.8%), Greenland periphery (~11.4%), and Southern Andes (~9.9%), while also plotting specific mass-change rates. However, it omits the required relative mass losses as percentages of year-2000 ice volume, so the key rankings and values for Central Europe, Caucasus, New Zealand, North Asia, Western Canada/USA, and low latitudes are not demonstrated; several specific-rate estimates also differ noticeably from the target."
     },
     {
      "index": 2,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.2,
      "score": 24,
      "reasoning": "This is Mode A. The report provides quantitative pairwise method comparisons and uncertainty intervals, but it compares altimetry/gravimetry mainly against a pooled “DEM + glaciological” product rather than DEM differencing alone, and it does not reproduce the specified mean differences or the glaciological bias/range; its highlighted discrepancies also differ from the target pattern. Thus the relevant analysis is present but methodologically mismatched and quantitatively incomplete relative to the published result."
     },
     {
      "index": 3,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.3,
      "score": 0,
      "reasoning": "This is an objective visual/quantitative criterion. None of the AI-generated figures compares observations with IPCC/GlacierMIP2 or CMIP6 projections, shows emission scenarios through 2040/2100, or visualizes the required low-end exceedance and future scenario dependence; the cumulative plot stops at 2023 and contains observations only."
     }
